0.9
------
-Added a terminal frontend (tiger-term): renders the LCD in 24-bit
 color as half-blocks, quadrants, sextants, or braille depending on
 terminal size, no display server needed
-Fixed the codebase to compile with modern GCC (missing prototypes,
 implicit int, wrong printf formats on 64-bit, bad pointer casts in
 gencpu output)
-Replaced the libggi frontend with SDL2 (runs natively on Wayland
 and X11)
-Grayscale palette and LCD contrast now actually work
-Added frame pacing to approximate real TI-92 speed ("tickrate 0"
 to disable)
-Integer-scaled resizable window
-Modernized the Makefile (pkg-config, dropped stale i386 flags)

0.8.1
------
-Fixed command and debug prompts

0.8
------
-Acquired source from Jonas Minnberg and permission to GPL it
-No longer using gets() function
-Removed SVGA code
-Ported over to libggi
-Added command line option to specify ROM file on command line
